<title>BELGIUM: EU clears German/French reinsurance venture.</title>
<headline>EU clears German/French reinsurance venture.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission has cleared the proposed Prevoyance RE reinsurance joint venture between three French companies and German company Muenchener Re, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The Commission said that only the German firm was active in reinsurance, while the three French ones -- Mederic Prevoyance, Urrpimmec, the insurance body for French metal, mechanical and electric industries, and CRI Prevoyance -- are in insurance.</p>
<p>The joint venture would not create or strengthen any dominant positions for the companies involved, the statement said, meaning the Commission felt able to clear it.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
